WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:02.102
For more on this amazing

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.003
events that have transpired

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:03.937
over the last several days,

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:04.871
I want to bring in

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.806
Shark Tank Judge Kevin O'Leary,

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.441
who is the chairman of O'Leary Ventures

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.010
and is here to join us

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.911
What are you hoping to hear from

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.880
from President Biden?

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:16.950
Well, I think I know what he's going

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.084
to say.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.619
I think I don't think he'll say it

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.687
in the way I'm suggesting.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.155
But what effectively happened

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.590
over the weekend

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.558
is that he national eyes

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.560
the American banking system.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.662
It's no longer a risk.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.998
It's no longer private in any sense.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.367
It is now backstopped by the government.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.002
Ultimately the taxpayer.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.705
So it doesn't matter how bad you are

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.373
as a bank manager.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.374
And a good example is

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.376
what happened in Silicon Valley back.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.377
That was a combination

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.312
of a negligent board of directors

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.914
and idiot management.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.382
That's very powerful cocktail

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.483
and put together.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.252
And it completely wiped out that bank.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.020
And that's what should have happened.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.622
And we knew before the weekend

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.990
started that every account

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.492
with $250,000 or less was insured.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.894
And anything beyond that,

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.695
which is generally business accounts

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.432
or sophisticated investors, was not.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:06.866
But that's all changed.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.802
Now, you have no risk in any bank

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:09.869
any time,

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.838
and you as a taxpayer bear

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.506
that going forward.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.874
When we spoke on Friday,

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:15.542
you said I said,

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.277
how big a deal is this, Kevin?

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.278
And we were taxing.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.279
You said next week

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:20.313
the real trouble starts

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.649
when they can't make payroll.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.483
Now it looks like

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:25.885
they will be making payroll,

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.387
I would imagine. So what do you think?

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.988
Do you think that

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.357
maybe the you know, the pressure is off

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:31.891
now that things

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.093
are going to go back to normal

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.627
or is there still more fallout here

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.997
No, they'll never go back to normal.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.833
Two things are going to happen.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.302
This this quick memo of this policy

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.236
decision

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.972
was to try and stop a run on small banks

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.607
mid-term midsize banks.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:48.775
I don't think long term

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:49.676
that's going to work

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.376
because why would

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.178
you take even 1% of risk

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.246
keeping your money,

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.547
or at least all of it

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:55.882
in a small regional bank?

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.016
You're going to diversify.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.418
And I think that's the first lesson

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.720
that wasn't being adhered to

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.723
is when you have liquid assets,

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.225
you want to make sure it's diversified

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.793
and the rule we've put in place

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.594
for our portfolio

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.295
companies is no more than 20%

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.498
in any one financial institution

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:12.732
because you never know

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.801
where the Black Swan is swimming.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:15.969
In other words,

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.837
every single institution

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.439
has an idiot manager,

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:20.607
big one, small ones.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:22.475
That's been proven by history.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.177
You just don't know where they are.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:24.911
And that's the same

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.246
for every sector of the economy.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:27.914
But the banking system is different.

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.083
We have 11 sectors in our economy,

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.152
the banking system, financial services

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.019
is one of them,

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.288
but it services all other ten

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.422
So what's really happening

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.056
when the president

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.224
steps out in a few moments

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.993
is he's basically saying, Look,

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.427
I can't take this risk anymore.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.629
I'm just going to nationalize

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:43.596
the whole thing.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.230
And that's the way

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.099
we should look at banking going forward.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:46.833
Nothing more

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:50.270
than highly regulated utilities.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.105
And that has profound impacts

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.640
for you as an investor.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.240
If you thought

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.542
putting your money into bank

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:56.643
stocks was a good idea,

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.510
you should change your mind

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.845
this morning forever.

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.947
And should you own bank bonds? Never.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.115
You were taught that lesson

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:02.849
over the weekend.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:05.318
If you own equity in Silicon Valley Bank,

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:06.619
it's worthless

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.688
if you all the bonds is worthless.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.289
Kevin, I.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:10.790
Go ahead.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.524
Sorry to interrupt, Kevin.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:11.791
I just

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.092
I do want to push back on that

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.460
because you've got to differentiate

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.296
between the small and medium sized banks

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.397
that were given

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.998
more lax requirements

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.166
in that 2018

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.734
legislation and the big guys

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.037
because the big guys closed up on Friday

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.271
and there's a flight

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.006
to safety, to JPMorgan,

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.776
to Citigroup, etc.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.012
That doesn't mean they're you know,

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.347
you should not assume

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:35.315
that just because they're big

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:38.318
they can't fail managers makes mistakes.

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.753
No, but they are. It's your big wait.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.789
But they are held to stress

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:43.957
test requirements,

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:45.892
higher capital and liquidity requirements

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:46.893
because of Dodd-Frank.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:47.760
That didn't

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.929
get diminished for those big ones.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.132
And you should assume

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:55.235
that stage is going to be lifted

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.102
even higher on them.

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:56.703
So they're going to be

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.004
even more regulated

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.939
as they become more concentrated

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.741
and far less profitable.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.009
That's my point.

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.410
This really does

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.612
make you think about owning

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.313
bank stocks long term.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.881
I think they'll be underperforming

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.250
the index for decades to come.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.851
That's my personal opinion,

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.486
but it's the behavior of you

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.188
as an investor in the actual accounts.

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:16.422
If you're a business,

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:17.657
you can't put it all in one

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.058
financial institutions

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.927
Certainly everybody learned that lesson

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:21.961
over the weekend.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.063
So diversification is going to matter.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.865
But this has fundamentally changed

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.333
the way you should look at banking

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.535
because I'm not really comfortable

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.436
that all of a sudden

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.105
we've de-risked everybody

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.373
all of the time.

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:36.876
It was a good idea to de-risk $250,000

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.911
and make more sophisticated investors

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.013
think about their behavior

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:41.281
and how they should put their capital

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:43.116
to work. Get diversity.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.317
You don't have to do that anymore.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:44.884
According to what

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.252
the President is going to say,

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.854
you have zero risk

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.889
and that has consequences.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.091
There's no such thing as a free lunch,

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.860
and this is going to be very expensive

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.928
for shareholders of banks long term.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:56.229
All right.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.864
I would never put my money into a bank

00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:59.132
stock ever again.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.267
Oh, Kevin O'Leary, Kevin,

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.769
I always appreciate your perspective.

